2026-10-15 03:23:29,185 DEBUG: Chroma query output: {'ids': [['sluPolicy_tailgating_14', 'sluPolicy_tailgating_4', 'sluPolicy_unmanned_aerial_sys_policy_1', 'sluPolicy_tailgating_3', 'sluPolicy_tailgating_15', 'sluPolicy_unmanned_aerial_sys_policy_7', 'sluPolicy_unmanned_aerial_sys_policy_0', 'sluPolicy_tailgating_2']], 'embeddings': None, 'documents': [['. Such vehicles should be used as a mode of transportation to the tailgating location and parked for the duration of the tailgating activity except when moving to and from campus. Non-licensed vehicles are not to be parked on sidewalks, shall not be parked where it can cause damage to grass or landscape and must always yield to pedestrians. • Non-licensed vehicles considered “street legal” may be operated on campus streets and can be parked in an identified parking space', '. All sound must be terminated at the start of the game. Noise amplification and music must be kept to a reasonable level. Only Clean Music/Radio Version may be played at tailgate. • Soliciting or selling goods/services will not be permitted on stadium grounds without prior approval from the university. • Except as may be specifically authorized by University Police, the operation of drones/unmanned aircraft systems on University property is prohibited', '. Purpose of Policy To establish requirements for the safe operation of unmanned aerial systems, also referred to as “drones”, on or above Southeastern Louisiana University property. Applicability This policy applies to the operation of all unmanned aerial systems, owned or leased, by University employees, students, contractors, or visitors. Policy Procedure A. Definitions 1', '. • Setting up, marking off, or holding a tailgate space in Friendship Circle without a tailgate prior approval from the Director for Athletics is prohibited. • Digging or any form of staking to secure tents is strictly prohibited without consent from the Director for the Physical Plant. • Amplified sound, including but not limited to radio station vans, live bands, DJs, televisions, sound systems, small battery-powered devices, is permitted with approval by the Director for Athletics', '. A non-licensed vehicle not parked in an identified parking space cannot be parked on sidewalks, shall not be parked where it can cause damage to grass or landscape and must always yield to pedestrians. • For purpose of this policy, Ned McGehee Drive (Friendship Circle) from McClimans Hall to Dyson Hall is considered pedestrian during tailgating activities', '. 4. UPD personnel will contact the Hammond Northshore Regional Airport air traffic control tower to ensure flight plan approval, prior to granting permission for a UAS operation. 5. No recreational UAS flights will be approved on or above Southeastern Louisiana University property. North Oak Park is exempt from this restriction under the following conditions: a) No university sanctioned athletic events are occurring at the time of flight', 'Responsible Administrator: VP Admin/Finance Responsible Office: Environmental Health & Safety Effective Date: 06/05/2018 Approved by: President Date of Revision: 06/05/2018 Date Reviewed (no substantive changes): 12/02/2025 Unmanned Aerial System Policy Policy Statement The University will adhere to all federal and state laws and regulations pertaining to the operation of unmanned aerial vehicles. We are committed to reducing and/or eliminating unnecessary risk to individuals and the agency', '. General • Although tailgating will be permitted on campus, certain areas may be designated to tailgate or designated for specific groups. • Tailgating will be limited to athletic events throughout campus. The University President reserves the right to designate areas of campus as non-tailgating locations. • Areas of campus may be reserved for specific university needs or events and will not be available for all game days']], 'uris': None, 'included': ['metadatas', 'documents', 'distances'], 'data': None, 'metadata